/-!
# Finite coproducts of sheafified representables as a covering set

Let `C` be a site and let `B ⊆ Ob(C)` be a subset. Consider the set `S` of those sheaves of sets
which have the form `K = ∐_{i = 1, …, n} h_{U_i}^#` with `U_1, …, U_n ∈ B`. Stacks 0GN4 asks when
`S` satisfies the hypotheses of Stacks 0GN3, and answers that the following four conditions on `B`
suffice:

1. for some `n ≥ 0` and `U_1, …, U_n ∈ B` the map `∐_i h_{U_i}^# ⟶ *` is surjective;
2. every covering of a `U ∈ B` can be refined by a covering `{U_i ⟶ U}_{i = 1, …, n}` with
   `U_i ∈ B`;
3. given `U, U' ∈ B` there are `n ≥ 0`, objects `U_1, …, U_n ∈ B` and maps `U_i ⟶ U`, `U_i ⟶ U'`
   such that `∐_i h_{U_i}^# ⟶ h_U^# ⨯ h_{U'}^#` is surjective;
4. given `a, b : U ⟶ U'` with `U, U' ∈ B` there are `U_1, …, U_n ∈ B` and maps `U_i ⟶ U`
   equalizing `a` and `b` such that `∐_i h_{U_i}^# ⟶ Equalizer(h_a^#, h_b^#)` is surjective.

Condition (2) alone already makes every member of `B` a quasi-compact object of the site, hence
every member of `S` a quasi-compact sheaf by Stacks 0GMQ; that is the fifth hypothesis of
Stacks 0GN3. The remaining four hypotheses of Stacks 0GN3 are obtained from (1), (2), (3) and (4)
respectively, the second of them by refining, over each summand of a `K ∈ S`, the sieve of local
liftings of the tautological section.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Cohomology.ColimitsOfCohomology.FiniteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda`: the set `S` of finite
  coproducts of sheafified representables of objects of `B`.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.ColimitsOfCohomology.HasFiniteCoverRefinementsFrom`: condition (2) at a single
  object, that every covering sieve of it is refined by a finite covering family whose sources
  belong to `B`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Cohomology.ColimitsOfCohomology.isQuasiCompactObject_of_hasFiniteCoverRefinementsFrom`:
  condition (2) makes an object of the site quasi-compact.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.ColimitsOfCohomology.isQuasiCompact_of_finiteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda`:
  **Stacks 0GN4, the quasi-compactness assertion.** Under (2) every member of `S` is a
  quasi-compact sheaf.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.ColimitsOfCohomology`
  `.isIso_colimit_post_rightDerived_globalSections_of_finite_covers`:
  **Stacks 0GN4, the criterion.** Conditions (1)–(4) give the conclusion of Stacks 0GN3, that
  `colim_λ H^p(C, F_λ) ⟶ H^p(C, colim_λ F_λ)` is an isomorphism.

## Implementation notes

A finite family is indexed by `Fin n`, with `n = 0` allowed, so that the empty coproduct is a
member of `S` and condition (1) is stated exactly as in the source. Refinement of a covering sieve
is expressed by inclusion of the sieve generated by the refining family, so the formulation does
not depend on a choice of pretopology presenting the site.

The two definitions and the quasi-compactness assertion hold for a site with an arbitrary morphism
universe. The criterion inherits the small-site convention of Stacks 0GN3: the site, the
coefficients and the index category of the filtered diagram all live in one universe.

Two parallel definitions of a quasi-compact object of `Sh(C)` are in play, `Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact`
(finite subsets and local surjectivity) and `Sheaf.QuasiCompact` (finite subsets as `Finset`s and
epimorphisms); the coproduct lemma Stacks 0GMQ is stated for the second and Stacks 0GN3 consumes
the first, so `Sheaf.quasiCompact_iff_isQuasiCompact` of
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.QuasiCompact.FiniteCoproducts` is used to pass between them.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GN4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GN4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GN3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GN3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GMQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GMQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D06](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D06)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace Stacks.Cohomology.ColimitsOfCohomology

universe v u

/-- Sheaves of sets on a site have colimits of the size of the site; the instance is needed to
form the coproducts below and to compare them with colimits in presheaves, and is local to each
file that uses it. -/
noncomputable local instance sheafOfTypes_hasColimitsOfSize {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C]
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) :
    HasColimitsOfSize.{max u v, max u v} (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) :=
  Sheaf.instHasColimitsOfSize

/-! ### The set `S` and the refinement condition -/

section Site

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- The sheaves of sets which are finite coproducts `∐_{i = 1, …, n} h_{U_i}^#` of sheafified
representables of objects of `B`, with `n = 0` allowed. This is the set `S` of Stacks 0GN4. -/
def FiniteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C]
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (B : Set C) : Set (Sheaf J (Type max u v)) :=
  {K | ∃ (n : ℕ) (U : Fin n → C),
    (∀ i, U i ∈ B) ∧ Nonempty (K ≅ ∐ fun i => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U i))}

/-- Every covering sieve of `U` is refined by a finite covering family `{V_i ⟶ U}_{i = 1, …, n}`
whose sources `V_i` belong to `B`. This is condition (2) of Stacks 0GN4, at the single object
`U`. -/
def HasFiniteCoverRefinementsFrom {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C]
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (B : Set C) (U : C) : Prop :=
  ∀ S : Sieve U, S ∈ J U →
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (V : Fin n → C) (p : ∀ i, V i ⟶ U),
      (∀ i, V i ∈ B) ∧ Sieve.ofArrows V p ∈ J U ∧ Sieve.ofArrows V p ≤ S

/-- Indexing a finite family of arrows by `ULift (Fin n)` does not change the sieve it generates. -/
private lemma ofArrows_ulift_eq {n : ℕ} {U : C} (V : Fin n → C) (p : ∀ i, V i ⟶ U) :
    Sieve.ofArrows (fun i : ULift (Fin n) => V i.down) (fun i => p i.down) =
      Sieve.ofArrows V p := by
  ext W f
  rw [Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff, Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨i, a, h⟩; exact ⟨i.down, a, h⟩
  · rintro ⟨i, a, h⟩; exact ⟨ULift.up i, a, h⟩

/-- An object whose coverings are all refined by finite covering families is a quasi-compact object
of the site (Stacks 090H): the refining family is itself the required refinement, and its index
type being finite, the index map into the given family has finite image.

This is the implication, used in Stacks 0GN4, by which condition (2) makes every element of `B`
quasi-compact. -/
theorem isQuasiCompactObject_of_hasFiniteCoverRefinementsFrom {B : Set C} {U : C}
    (h : HasFiniteCoverRefinementsFrom J B U) : J.IsQuasiCompactObject U := by
  intro 𝒰 h𝒰
  obtain ⟨n, V, p, _, hcov, hle⟩ := h 𝒰.sieve₀ h𝒰
  let 𝒱 : PreZeroHypercover.{max u v} U :=
    { I₀ := ULift.{max u v} (Fin n), X := fun i => V i.down, f := fun i => p i.down }
  classical
  have hx (i : Fin n) : ∃ (j : 𝒰.I₀) (a : V i ⟶ 𝒰.X j), p i = a ≫ 𝒰.f j :=
    (Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff _ _ _).1 (hle (p i) (Sieve.ofArrows_mk V p i))
  choose j a ha using hx
  have hhom : 𝒱.Hom 𝒰 :=
    { s₀ := fun i => j i.down, h₀ := fun i => a i.down, w₀ := fun i => (ha i.down).symm }
  refine ⟨𝒱, hhom, ?_, Set.finite_range _⟩
  rw [show 𝒱.sieve₀ = Sieve.ofArrows V p from ofArrows_ulift_eq V p]; exact hcov

-- The two spellings of a quasi-compact sheaf are compared once and for all in
-- `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/QuasiCompact/FiniteCoproducts.lean`, by
-- `Sheaf.quasiCompact_of_isQuasiCompact` (line 645) and
-- `Sheaf.isQuasiCompact_of_quasiCompact` (line 677); the private copies that used to stand
-- here were the same two statements and have been removed in favour of them.

/-- An initial sheaf is quasi-compact: the empty subfamily already surjects onto it, because any
two maps out of an initial object agree. -/
private lemma isQuasiCompact_of_isInitial (F : Sheaf J (Type max u v)) (hF : IsInitial F) :
    Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact F := by
  intro I G f hf
  exact ⟨∅, Set.finite_empty, (Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi _).2
    ⟨fun g h _ => hF.hom_ext g h⟩⟩

/-- **Stacks 0GN4, quasi-compactness assertion.** If every covering of every `U ∈ B` is refined by
a finite covering family with sources in `B` — condition (2) — then every finite coproduct of
sheafified representables of objects of `B` is a quasi-compact sheaf.

Condition (2) makes each `U ∈ B` a quasi-compact object of the site, hence each `h_U^#` a
quasi-compact sheaf by Stacks 0D06, and a finite coproduct of quasi-compact sheaves is
quasi-compact by Stacks 0GMQ. The empty coproduct is handled separately, being initial. -/
@[stacks 0GN4 "quasi-compactness assertion"]
theorem isQuasiCompact_of_finiteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C]
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (B : Set C)
    (h_refine : ∀ U ∈ B, HasFiniteCoverRefinementsFrom J B U)
    {K : Sheaf J (Type max u v)} (hK : K ∈ FiniteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda J B) :
    Sheaf.IsQuasiCompact K := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨n, U, hU, ⟨e⟩⟩ := hK
  refine Sheaf.isQuasiCompact_of_isLocallySurjective e.symm.hom (by infer_instance) ?_
  by_cases hn : n = 0
  · subst n
    let D := Discrete.functor (fun i : Fin 0 => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U i))
    exact isQuasiCompact_of_isInitial _ (IsInitial.ofUniqueHom
      (fun Z => colimit.desc D ⟨Z, ⟨fun i => Fin.elim0 i.as, by intro i; exact Fin.elim0 i.as⟩⟩)
      fun _ _ => colimit.hom_ext fun i => Fin.elim0 i.as)
  · exact Sheaf.isQuasiCompact_of_quasiCompact
      (Sheaf.quasiCompact_coproduct_fin (J := J) (n := n) (Nat.one_le_iff_ne_zero.mpr hn) _
        fun i => Sheaf.quasiCompact_of_isQuasiCompact
          ((GrothendieckTopology.isQuasiCompactObject_iff_isQuasiCompact_sheafifiedYoneda
            J (U i)).1 (isQuasiCompactObject_of_hasFiniteCoverRefinementsFrom
              (h_refine (U i) (hU i)))))

section

open Opposite

/-! ### Nested finite coproducts -/

/-- A coproduct of sheafified representables of objects of `B`, indexed by a finite type, is a
finite coproduct in the sense of `FiniteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda`. -/
private lemma coproduct_mem_finiteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda {B : Set C} {γ : Type*}
    [Finite γ] [HasColimitsOfShape (Discrete γ) (Sheaf J (Type max u v))]
    (Y : γ → C) (hY : ∀ z, Y z ∈ B) :
    (∐ fun z => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (Y z)) ∈ FiniteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda J B := by
  classical
  let : Fintype γ := Fintype.ofFinite γ
  let e : Fin (Fintype.card γ) ≃ γ := (Fintype.equivFin γ).symm
  exact ⟨Fintype.card γ, fun i => Y (e i), fun i => hY _,
    ⟨(Sigma.reindex e (fun z => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (Y z))).symm⟩⟩

/-- A coproduct of finitely many finite coproducts of sheafified representables of objects of `B`
is again a finite coproduct of such, the index type being the sigma type of the two layers.

This is the general-site form of a private lemma of
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.FilteredColimits.FiniteCoproductsOfRepresentables`. -/
lemma nestedFiniteCoproduct_mem (B : Set C) {α : Type max u v} [Finite α]
    (β : α → Type max u v) [∀ a, Finite (β a)] (X : ∀ a, β a → C)
    (hX : ∀ a b, X a b ∈ B) :
    (∐ fun a => ∐ fun b => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (X a b)) ∈
      FiniteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda J B := by
  obtain ⟨n, Z, hZ, ⟨e⟩⟩ := coproduct_mem_finiteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda (J := J) (B := B)
    (fun z : Σ a, β a => X z.1 z.2) fun z => hX z.1 z.2
  exact ⟨n, Z, hZ, ⟨(sigmaSigmaIso β fun i j => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (X i j)).trans e⟩⟩

/-! ### Sections of sheafifications of representables -/

/-- The section of a sheafification corresponding to the sheafification of a map out of a
representable presheaf: it is the image under `toSheafify` of the section the map picks out. -/
lemma sectionEquiv_presheafToSheaf_map {X : C}
    {P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v} (f : uliftYoneda.{u}.obj X ⟶ P) :
    Sheaf.sectionEquiv J ((presheafToSheaf J (Type max u v)).map f) =
      (toSheafify J P).app (op X) (f.app (op X) (ULift.up (𝟙 X))) := by
  show uliftYonedaEquiv.{u}
    ((sheafificationAdjunction J (Type max u v)).homEquiv
      (uliftYoneda.{u}.obj X) ((presheafToSheaf J (Type max u v)).obj P)
      ((presheafToSheaf J (Type max u v)).map f)) = _
  rw [← Category.comp_id ((presheafToSheaf J (Type max u v)).map f),
    (sheafificationAdjunction J (Type max u v)).homEquiv_naturality_left f (𝟙 _)]
  rfl

/-- A map `p : V ⟶ U` lies in the sieve of local liftings, along `f`, of the section of `G`
corresponding to `x : h_U^# ⟶ G` exactly when `h_p^# ≫ x` factors through `f`. -/
lemma mem_imageSieve_sectionEquiv_iff {F G : Sheaf J (Type max u v)}
    (f : F ⟶ G) {U V : C} (x : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj U ⟶ G)
    (p : V ⟶ U) :
    Presheaf.imageSieve f.hom (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J x) p ↔
      ∃ y : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj V ⟶ F,
        y ≫ f = (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map p ≫ x := by
  show (∃ t, f.hom.app (op V) t = G.obj.map p.op (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J x)) ↔ _
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨t, ht⟩
    refine ⟨(Sheaf.sectionEquiv J).symm t, (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J).injective ?_⟩
    rwa [Sheaf.sectionEquiv_map_comp, Sheaf.sectionEquiv_comp, Equiv.apply_symm_apply]
  · rintro ⟨y, hy⟩
    refine ⟨Sheaf.sectionEquiv J y, ?_⟩
    have h := congrArg (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J) hy
    rwa [Sheaf.sectionEquiv_map_comp, Sheaf.sectionEquiv_comp] at h

/-- Pulling back the sieve of local liftings of a section corresponding to `x : h_U^# ⟶ G` along
`p : V ⟶ U` gives the sieve of local liftings of the section corresponding to `h_p^# ≫ x`. -/
lemma pullback_imageSieve_sectionEquiv {F G : Sheaf J (Type max u v)}
    (f : F ⟶ G) {U V : C} (x : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj U ⟶ G)
    (p : V ⟶ U) :
    (Presheaf.imageSieve f.hom (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J x)).pullback p =
      Presheaf.imageSieve f.hom
        (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map p ≫ x)) := by
  rw [Presheaf.pullback_imageSieve, Sheaf.sectionEquiv_map_comp]

/-! ### Transport along an equality of indices -/

/-- Transport of an equality of composites along an equality of indices: if `g ≫ a` and `g ≫ b` are
heterogeneously equal, with `a : U ⟶ V i` and `b : U ⟶ V j` for `i = j`, then `g ≫ a` equals the
transport of `g ≫ b`. -/
lemma comp_eq_cast_of_heq {ι : Type*} {V : ι → C} {U W : C}
    {i j : ι} {a : U ⟶ V i} {b : U ⟶ V j} (h : i = j) (g : W ⟶ U)
    (hab : HEq (g ≫ a) (g ≫ b)) :
    g ≫ a = g ≫ Eq.mp (congrArg (fun j => U ⟶ V j) h.symm) b := by
  subst j
  exact eq_of_heq hab

/-- Transporting an arrow along an equality of indices does not change the composite of its
sheafified representable with the coproduct inclusion. -/
lemma sheafifiedYoneda_map_cast_comp_sigma_ι {m : ℕ} (V : Fin m → C)
    {U : C} {i j : Fin m} (h : i = j) (b : U ⟶ V j) :
    (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (Eq.mp (congrArg (fun j => U ⟶ V j) h.symm) b) ≫
        Sigma.ι (fun k => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V k)) i =
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map b ≫
        Sigma.ι (fun k => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V k)) j := by
  subst j
  rfl

/-! ### Maps into a finite coproduct of sheafified representables -/

/-- A finite coproduct of sheafified representables is the sheafification of the coproduct of the
representable presheaves, compatibly with sections: the section of the sheafification given by a
map `t : W ⟶ V k` followed by the `k`-th inclusion is the image under `toSheafify` of the `k`-th
inclusion of `t`. -/
private lemma exists_iso_sectionEquiv_sigma_ι {m : ℕ} (V : Fin m → C) :
    ∃ e : (∐ fun i : Fin m => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V i)) ≅
        (presheafToSheaf J (Type max u v)).obj (∐ fun i : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V i)),
      ∀ {W : C} (k : Fin m) (t : W ⟶ V k),
        Sheaf.sectionEquiv J ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map t ≫
            Sigma.ι (fun i : Fin m => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V i)) k ≫ e.hom) =
          (toSheafify J (∐ fun i : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V i))).app (op W)
            ((Sigma.ι (fun i : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V i)) k).app (op W) (ULift.up t)) := by
  classical
  let F := presheafToSheaf J (Type max u v)
  let : PreservesColimit (Discrete.functor fun i : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V i)) F :=
    (sheafificationAdjunction J (Type max u v)).leftAdjoint_preservesColimits
      |>.preservesColimitsOfShape.preservesColimit
  let e : (∐ fun i : Fin m => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V i)) ≅
      F.obj (∐ fun i : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V i)) :=
    (PreservesCoproduct.iso F (fun i : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V i))).symm
  refine ⟨e, fun k t => ?_⟩
  have hι : Sigma.ι (fun i : Fin m => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V i)) k ≫ e.hom =
      F.map (Sigma.ι (fun i : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V i)) k) :=
    ι_comp_sigmaComparison (G := F) (f := fun i : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V i)) k
  have hmap : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map t ≫
      F.map (Sigma.ι (fun i : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V i)) k) =
      F.map (uliftYoneda.{u}.map t ≫ Sigma.ι (fun i : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V i)) k) :=
    (F.map_comp _ _).symm
  rw [hι, hmap, sectionEquiv_presheafToSheaf_map]
  congr 1
  simp

/-- A map `h_U^# ⟶ ∐_{i < m} h_{V_i}^#` into a finite coproduct of sheafified representables
factors, locally on `U`, through one of the summands by a map of the site.

The coproduct is the sheafification of the coproduct of representable presheaves, so the section of
it corresponding to the given map lifts locally to the presheaf coproduct, whose sections are
jointly covered by the summands. -/
lemma exists_local_factor_through_finite_coproduct {m : ℕ} {U : C}
    (V : Fin m → C) (f : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj U ⟶
      ∐ fun i : Fin m => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V i)) :
    ∃ S : Sieve U, S ∈ J U ∧
      ∀ ⦃W : C⦄ (g : W ⟶ U), S g →
        ∃ i : Fin m, ∃ h : W ⟶ V i,
          (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map g ≫ f =
            (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map h ≫
              Sigma.ι (fun i : Fin m => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V i)) i := by
  classical
  let P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v := ∐ fun i : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V i)
  let F := presheafToSheaf J (Type max u v)
  let D : Discrete (Fin m) ⥤ (Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v) :=
    Discrete.functor (fun i : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V i))
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_iso_sectionEquiv_sigma_ι (J := J) V
  let x := Sheaf.sectionEquiv J (f ≫ e.hom)
  refine ⟨Presheaf.imageSieve (toSheafify J P) x,
    Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J (toSheafify J P) x, ?_⟩
  intro W g hg
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := hg
  let E := evaluation (Cᵒᵖ) (Type max u v)
  let eW := colimitObjIsoColimitCompEvaluation D (op W)
  obtain ⟨⟨i⟩, y, hy⟩ :=
    Types.jointly_surjective (D ⋙ E.obj (op W)) (colimit.isColimit _) (eW.hom z)
  have hzrep : z = (colimit.ι D (Discrete.mk i)).app (op W) y := by
    have hy' := congrArg eW.inv hy
    have hι' := colimitObjIsoColimitCompEvaluation_ι_inv D (Discrete.mk i) (op W)
    have hι'' := congrArg (fun k => k y) hι'
    simpa using hy'.symm.trans hι''
  rcases y with ⟨h⟩
  refine ⟨i, h, ?_⟩
  have hleft :
      Sheaf.sectionEquiv J ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map g ≫ f ≫ e.hom) =
        (F.obj P).obj.map g.op x := by
    rw [Sheaf.sectionEquiv_map_comp]
  have hright :
      Sheaf.sectionEquiv J
          ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map h ≫
          Sigma.ι (fun i : Fin m => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V i)) i ≫ e.hom) =
        (F.obj P).obj.map g.op x := by
    rw [he]
    have hsection : (Sigma.ι (fun i : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V i)) i).app (op W)
        (ULift.up h) = (colimit.ι D (Discrete.mk i)).app (op W) (ULift.up h) := by
      simp [D]
    rw [hsection, ← hzrep]
    exact hz
  have hcomp : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map g ≫ f ≫ e.hom =
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map h ≫
        Sigma.ι (fun i : Fin m => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V i)) i ≫ e.hom :=
    (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J).injective (hleft.trans hright.symm)
  apply (cancel_mono e.hom).1
  simpa only [Category.assoc] using hcomp

/-- Two maps of the site into the summands of a finite coproduct of sheafified representables
whose composites with the coproduct inclusions agree have, locally on the source, the same index
and the same composite. -/
lemma exists_local_eq_through_finite_coproduct {m : ℕ} {U : C}
    (V : Fin m → C) {i j : Fin m} {a : U ⟶ V i} {b : U ⟶ V j}
    (h : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map a ≫
        Sigma.ι (fun k : Fin m => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V k)) i =
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map b ≫
        Sigma.ι (fun k : Fin m => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V k)) j) :
    ∃ S : Sieve U, S ∈ J U ∧
      ∀ ⦃W : C⦄ (g : W ⟶ U), S g → ∃ _ : i = j, HEq (g ≫ a) (g ≫ b) := by
  classical
  let P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type max u v := ∐ fun k : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V k)
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_iso_sectionEquiv_sigma_ι (J := J) V
  let E := evaluation (Cᵒᵖ) (Type max u v)
  let x : ToType (P.obj (op U)) :=
    (E.obj (op U)).map (Sigma.ι (fun k : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V k)) i) (ULift.up a)
  let y : ToType (P.obj (op U)) :=
    (E.obj (op U)).map (Sigma.ι (fun k : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V k)) j) (ULift.up b)
  have hxy :
      Sheaf.sectionEquiv J ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map a ≫
        Sigma.ι (fun k : Fin m => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V k)) i ≫ e.hom) =
      Sheaf.sectionEquiv J ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map b ≫
        Sigma.ι (fun k : Fin m => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V k)) j ≫ e.hom) := by
    exact congrArg (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J) (congrArg (fun z => z ≫ e.hom) h)
  have hxy' : (toSheafify J P).app (op U) x = (toSheafify J P).app (op U) y :=
    (he i a).symm.trans (hxy.trans (he j b))
  let S := Presheaf.equalizerSieve x y
  refine ⟨S, Presheaf.equalizerSieve_mem J (toSheafify J P) x y hxy', ?_⟩
  intro W g hg
  rw [Presheaf.equalizerSieve_apply] at hg
  let Q : Fin m → Type max u v := fun k => (E.obj (op W)).obj (uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V k))
  let eW : P.obj (op W) ≅ ∐ Q :=
    PreservesCoproduct.iso (E.obj (op W)) (fun k : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V k))
  have hιW₀ (k : Fin m) :
      Sigma.ι Q k ≫ eW.inv = (E.obj (op W)).map
        (Sigma.ι (fun l : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V l)) k) :=
    ι_comp_sigmaComparison (G := E.obj (op W)) (f := fun l : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V l)) k
  have hιW (k : Fin m) :
      (E.obj (op W)).map
        (Sigma.ι (fun l : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V l)) k) ≫ eW.hom = Sigma.ι Q k := by
    rw [← hιW₀]
    simp
  have hside (k : Fin m) (t : U ⟶ V k) :
      eW.hom ((P.map g.op)
        ((Sigma.ι (fun l : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V l)) k).app
          (op U) (ULift.up t))) = Sigma.ι Q k (ULift.up (g ≫ t)) := by
    let ι := Sigma.ι (fun l : Fin m => uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (V l)) k
    have hn : (P.map g.op) (ι.app (op U) (ULift.up t)) =
        ι.app (op W) (ULift.up (g ≫ t)) := by
      simpa [ConcreteCategory.comp_apply] using
        congrArg (fun z => z (ULift.up t)) (ι.naturality g.op).symm
    rw [hn]
    exact congrArg (fun z => z (ULift.up (g ≫ t))) (hιW k)
  have hq : Sigma.ι Q i (ULift.up (g ≫ a)) = Sigma.ι Q j (ULift.up (g ≫ b)) := by
    calc
      Sigma.ι Q i (ULift.up (g ≫ a)) = eW.hom ((P.map g.op) x) := (hside i a).symm
      _ = eW.hom ((P.map g.op) y) := congrArg eW.hom hg
      _ = Sigma.ι Q j (ULift.up (g ≫ b)) := hside j b
  let c : Cofan Q := Cofan.mk (∐ Q) (Sigma.ι Q)
  have hc : IsColimit c := coproductIsCoproduct Q
  obtain rfl : i = j := Cofan.eq_of_inj_apply_eq_of_isColimit (c := c) hc _ _ hq
  exact ⟨rfl, heq_of_eq (ULift.up.inj (Cofan.inj_injective_of_isColimit (c := c) hc i hq))⟩

end

end Site

/-! ### The criterion -/

section SmallSite

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- Global sections of abelian sheaves on a small site is an additive functor; the instance is
needed to speak of its right derived functors and is local to each file that does. -/
noncomputable local instance abelianSheafGlobalSections_additive {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C]
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) : (Sheaf.Γ J (Ab.{u})).Additive :=
  Functor.additive_of_preserves_binary_products _

/-- Local surjectivity of `f₃ = f₁ ≫ f₂` is equivalent to local surjectivity of `f₂` once `f₁` is
locally surjective. The sheaf-level form of `Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_of_fac`. -/
private lemma isLocallySurjective_iff_of_comp_eq {F₁ F₂ F₃ : Sheaf J (Type u)}
    {f₁ : F₁ ⟶ F₂} {f₂ : F₂ ⟶ F₃} {f₃ : F₁ ⟶ F₃} (fac : f₁ ≫ f₂ = f₃)
    [Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective f₁] :
    Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective f₃ ↔ Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective f₂ := by
  refine Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_of_fac J (f₁ := f₁.hom) (f₃ := f₃.hom) ?_
  rw [← ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom, fac]

/-- A family `{X_i ⟶ S}` generates a covering sieve of `S` exactly when the induced map
`∐_i h_{X_i}^# ⟶ h_S^#` of sheafified representables is surjective. -/
private lemma isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_map_iff_ofArrows_mem
    {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {S : C} {ι : Type u}
    {X : ι → C} (p : ∀ i, X i ⟶ S) :
    Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Sigma.desc fun i ↦ (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i)) ↔
      Sieve.ofArrows X p ∈ J S := by
  have fac :
    (sigmaComparison (presheafToSheaf J (Type u)) fun i ↦ uliftYoneda.{u}.obj (X i)) ≫
        (presheafToSheaf J (Type u)).map
          (Sigma.desc fun i ↦ uliftYoneda.{u}.map (p i)) =
      Sigma.desc fun i ↦ (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i) :=
    sigmaComparison_map_desc _ _ _ _
  exact (isLocallySurjective_iff_of_comp_eq fac).trans
    ((Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_presheafToSheaf_map_iff J
        (Sigma.desc fun i ↦ uliftYoneda.{u}.map (p i))).trans
      (J.ofArrows_mem_iff_isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_uliftYoneda_map p).symm)








/-- **Stacks 0GN4, the criterion.** Let `C` be a small site and `B ⊆ Ob(C)`, and assume

1. for some `n ≥ 0` and `U_1, …, U_n ∈ B` the map `∐_i h_{U_i}^# ⟶ *` is surjective,
2. every covering of a `U ∈ B` is refined by a finite covering family with sources in `B`,
3. for any `U, U' ∈ B` there are finitely many `V_i ∈ B` with maps to both for which
   `∐_i h_{V_i}^# ⟶ h_U^# ⨯ h_{U'}^#` is surjective, and
4. for any `a, b : U ⟶ U'` between members of `B` there are finitely many `V_i ∈ B` with maps to
   `U` equalizing `a` and `b` for which `∐_i h_{V_i}^# ⟶ Equalizer(h_a^#, h_b^#)` is surjective.

Then `colim_λ H^p(C, F_λ) ⟶ H^p(C, colim_λ F_λ)` is an isomorphism in every degree, for every
filtered diagram of abelian sheaves.

The proof checks the five hypotheses of Stacks 0GN3 for the set `S` of finite coproducts of
sheafified representables of objects of `B`. Hypotheses (1), (3) and (4) of Stacks 0GN3 come from
(1), (3) and (4) here, after rewriting a coproduct of pairings as a map out of a coproduct and
distributing a coproduct over a product. Hypothesis (2), the lifting property for a surjection
`G ⟶ K` with `K ∈ S`, is obtained by applying (2) to the sieve of local liftings of the
tautological section of each summand of `K`: this produces a finite covering of each summand by
objects of `B` over which the surjection splits, and the resulting coproduct is again in `S`.
Hypothesis (5) is `isQuasiCompact_of_finiteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda`. -/
@[stacks 0GN4 "criterion"]
theorem isIso_colimit_post_rightDerived_globalSections_of_finite_covers
    {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (B : Set C)
    (h_terminal : ∃ (m : ℕ) (U : Fin m → C),
      (∀ i, U i ∈ B) ∧
        Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective
          (Sigma.desc fun i => terminal.from ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U i))))
    (h_refine : ∀ U ∈ B, HasFiniteCoverRefinementsFrom J B U)
    (h_product : ∀ U ∈ B, ∀ U' ∈ B,
      ∃ (m : ℕ) (V : Fin m → C),
        (∀ i, V i ∈ B) ∧ ∃ (p : ∀ i, V i ⟶ U) (q : ∀ i, V i ⟶ U'),
          Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Sigma.desc fun i =>
            prod.lift ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i))
              ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (q i))))
    (h_equalizer : ∀ {U U' : C} (a b : U ⟶ U'), U ∈ B → U' ∈ B →
      ∃ (m : ℕ) (V : Fin m → C),
        (∀ i, V i ∈ B) ∧ ∃ (p : ∀ i, V i ⟶ U) (hp : ∀ i, p i ≫ a = p i ≫ b),
          Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Sigma.desc fun i =>
            equalizer.lift (f := (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map a)
              (g := (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map b)
              ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i)) (by
              simpa only [Functor.map_comp] using congrArg (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (hp i))))
    (n : ℕ) {I : Type u} [SmallCategory I] [IsFiltered I]
    (F : I ⥤ Sheaf J (Ab.{u})) :
    IsIso (colimit.post F ((Sheaf.Γ J (Ab.{u})).rightDerived n)) := by
  classical
  let S := FiniteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda J B
  apply isIso_colimit_post_rightDerived_globalSections J S
  · obtain ⟨m, U, hU, hsurj⟩ := h_terminal
    let K := ∐ fun i : Fin m => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U i)
    have hsurj' : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (terminal.from K) :=
      (Subsingleton.elim (Sigma.desc (fun i : Fin m => terminal.from
        ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U i)))) (terminal.from K)) ▸ hsurj
    refine ⟨K, ?_, hsurj'⟩
    exact ⟨m, U, hU, ⟨Iso.refl _⟩⟩
  · intro G K f hK hsurj
    obtain ⟨n, U, hU, ⟨e⟩⟩ := hK
    let O := ULift (Fin n)
    let R := ∐ fun i : O => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U i.down)
    let e' : K ≅ R := e.trans (Sigma.reindex Equiv.ulift.symm
      (fun i : O => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U i.down)))
    let f' : G ⟶ R := f ≫ e'.hom
    have hf' : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective f' := by
      apply (Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi _).2
      have hfepi : Epi f := (Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi f).1 hsurj
      let : Epi f := hfepi
      exact epi_comp f e'.hom
    have hRef : ∀ i : Fin n, ∃ (m : ℕ) (V : Fin m → C) (p : ∀ j, V j ⟶ U i),
        (∀ j, V j ∈ B) ∧ Sieve.ofArrows V p ∈ J (U i) ∧
          Sieve.ofArrows V p ≤ Presheaf.imageSieve f'.hom
            ((Sigma.ι (fun k : O => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U k.down)) (ULift.up i)).hom.app
              (Opposite.op (U i)) (Sheaf.tautologicalSection J (U i))) := by
      intro i
      apply h_refine (U i) (hU i)
      exact Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J f'.hom
        ((Sigma.ι (fun k : O => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U k.down)) (ULift.up i)).hom.app
          (Opposite.op (U i)) (Sheaf.tautologicalSection J (U i)))
    choose m V p hV hVcov hVle using hRef
    let β : O → Type u := fun i => ULift (Fin (m i.down))
    let α := Σ i : O, β i
    have hSections : ∀ a : α, ∃ t : G.obj.obj (Opposite.op (V a.1.down a.2.down)),
        f'.hom.app (Opposite.op (V a.1.down a.2.down)) t =
          R.obj.map (p a.1.down a.2.down).op
            ((Sigma.ι (fun k : O => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U k.down)) a.1).hom.app
              (Opposite.op (U a.1.down)) (Sheaf.tautologicalSection J (U a.1.down))) := by
      intro a
      apply hVle a.1.down
      exact Sieve.ofArrows_mk (V a.1.down) (p a.1.down) a.2.down
    choose t ht using hSections
    let X : α → Sheaf J (Type u) := fun a =>
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V a.1.down a.2.down)
    let g₀ : ∀ a : α, X a ⟶ G := fun a => (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J).symm (t a)
    let q₀ : ∀ a : α, X a ⟶ R := fun a =>
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p a.1.down a.2.down) ≫
        Sigma.ι (fun k : O => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U k.down)) a.1
    have hfac₀ : ∀ a : α, g₀ a ≫ f' = q₀ a := by
      intro a
      apply (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J).injective
      simpa only [g₀, q₀, Sheaf.sectionEquiv_comp, Equiv.apply_symm_apply,
        Sheaf.sectionEquiv_sheafifiedYoneda_map, ← NatTrans.naturality_apply,
        Sheaf.map_op_tautologicalSection] using ht a
    let gᵢ : ∀ i : O, (∐ fun j : β i => X ⟨i, j⟩) ⟶ G :=
      fun i => Sigma.desc fun j => g₀ ⟨i, j⟩
    let hᵢ : ∀ i : O, (∐ fun j : β i => X ⟨i, j⟩) ⟶
        (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U i.down) :=
      fun i => Sigma.desc (f := fun j : β i => X ⟨i, j⟩) fun j =>
        (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i.down j.down)
    have hᵢepi : ∀ i : O, Epi (hᵢ i) := by
      intro i
      have hcovUL : Sieve.ofArrows (fun j : β i => V i.down j.down)
          (fun j => p i.down j.down) ∈ J (U i.down) := by
        rw [show Sieve.ofArrows (fun j : β i => V i.down j.down) (fun j => p i.down j.down) =
          Sieve.ofArrows (V i.down) (p i.down) from ofArrows_ulift_eq _ _]
        exact hVcov i.down
      have hl := (isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_map_iff_ofArrows_mem
        (S := U i.down) (X := fun j : β i => V i.down j.down)
        (p := fun j => p i.down j.down)).2 hcovUL
      exact (Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi _).1 (show Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (hᵢ i) from hl)
    let K' := ∐ fun i : O => ∐ fun j : β i => X ⟨i, j⟩
    let g : K' ⟶ G := Sigma.desc gᵢ
    let q : K' ⟶ R := Sigma.desc fun i => hᵢ i ≫
      Sigma.ι (fun k : O => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U k.down)) i
    have hq : q = Limits.Sigma.map hᵢ := rfl
    have hqepi : Epi q := by
      rw [hq]
      let : ∀ i : O, Epi (hᵢ i) := hᵢepi
      exact Limits.Sigma.map_epi hᵢ
    have hfac : g ≫ f' = q := by
      apply Sigma.hom_ext
      intro i
      apply Sigma.hom_ext
      intro j
      calc
        Sigma.ι (fun j : β i => X ⟨i, j⟩) j ≫
            Sigma.ι (fun k : O => ∐ fun j : β k => X ⟨k, j⟩) i ≫
              g ≫ f' = g₀ ⟨i, j⟩ ≫ f' := by simp [g, gᵢ]
        _ = q₀ ⟨i, j⟩ := hfac₀ ⟨i, j⟩
        _ = Sigma.ι (fun j : β i => X ⟨i, j⟩) j ≫
            Sigma.ι (fun k : O => ∐ fun j : β k => X ⟨k, j⟩) i ≫
              q := by simp only [q, q₀, hᵢ, ← Category.assoc, Sigma.ι_desc]
    have hmem : K' ∈ S := by
      let : Fintype O := inferInstance
      let : ∀ i : O, Fintype (β i) := fun _ => inferInstance
      simpa [K', X, α, β] using
        (nestedFiniteCoproduct_mem (B := B) (α := O) (β := β)
          (X := fun i j => V i.down j.down) (fun i j => hV i.down j.down))
    refine ⟨K', hmem, ⟨g, ?_⟩⟩
    apply (Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi _).2
    have hgf : g ≫ f = q ≫ e'.inv := by
      calc
        g ≫ f = (g ≫ f') ≫ e'.inv := by
          simp [f', Category.assoc, e'.hom_inv_id]
        _ = q ≫ e'.inv := by rw [hfac]
    rw [hgf]
    let : Epi q := hqepi
    exact epi_comp q e'.inv
  · intro K hK K' hK'
    obtain ⟨n, U, hU, ⟨e⟩⟩ := hK
    obtain ⟨n', U', hU', ⟨e'⟩⟩ := hK'
    let α := Fin n × Fin n'
    let choices : ∀ z : α, ∃ (m : ℕ) (V : Fin m → C),
        (∀ k, V k ∈ B) ∧ ∃ (p : ∀ k, V k ⟶ U z.1)
          (q : ∀ k, V k ⟶ U' z.2),
          Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Sigma.desc fun k =>
            prod.lift ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p k))
              ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (q k))) := by
      intro z
      exact h_product (U z.1) (hU z.1) (U' z.2) (hU' z.2)
    choose m V hV p q hsurj using choices
    let A : Fin n → Sheaf J (Type u) := fun i => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U i)
    let A' : Fin n' → Sheaf J (Type u) := fun i => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U' i)
    let P : α → Sheaf J (Type u) := fun z => A z.1 ⨯ A' z.2
    let β : α → Type u := fun z => ULift.{u} (Fin (m z))
    let E : α → Sheaf J (Type u) := fun z => ∐ fun k : β z =>
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V z k.down)
    let E₀ : α → Sheaf J (Type u) := fun z => ∐ fun k : Fin (m z) =>
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V z k)
    let eInner : ∀ z : α, E z ≅ E₀ z := fun z =>
      (Sigma.reindex Equiv.ulift.symm
        (fun k : ULift.{u} (Fin (m z)) => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (V z k.down))).symm
    let ep₀ : ∀ z : α, E₀ z ⟶ P z := fun z => Sigma.desc fun k =>
      prod.lift ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p z k))
        ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (q z k))
    let ep : ∀ z : α, E z ⟶ P z := fun z => (eInner z).hom ≫ ep₀ z
    let K'' := ∐ E
    let T := ∐ P
    let hpair : K'' ⟶ T := Limits.Sigma.map ep
    have hepiPair : Epi hpair := by
      let : ∀ z : α, Epi (ep z) := fun z =>
        by
          let : Epi (ep₀ z) :=
            (Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi (ep₀ z)).1 (hsurj z)
          let : Epi (eInner z).hom := inferInstance
          exact epi_comp (eInner z).hom (ep₀ z)
      exact Limits.Sigma.map_epi ep
    let tA : ∀ i : Fin n, A i ⟶ ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type u)) :=
      fun i => terminal.from (A i)
    let tA' : ∀ i : Fin n', A' i ⟶ ⊤_ (Sheaf J (Type u)) :=
      fun i => terminal.from (A' i)
    let compPull : (z : α) → pullback (terminal.from (A z.1))
        (terminal.from (A' z.2)) ⟶ pullback (Sigma.desc tA) (Sigma.desc tA') := fun z =>
      pullback.map (terminal.from (A z.1)) (terminal.from (A' z.2))
        (Sigma.desc tA) (Sigma.desc tA')
        (Sigma.ι A z.1) (Sigma.ι A' z.2) (𝟙 _)
        (by apply Subsingleton.elim) (by apply Subsingleton.elim)
    have hcompIso : IsIso (Sigma.desc compPull) :=
      FinitaryPreExtensive.isIso_sigmaDesc_map
        tA tA'
    have htA : Sigma.desc tA = terminal.from (∐ A) := Subsingleton.elim _ _
    have htA' : Sigma.desc tA' = terminal.from (∐ A') := Subsingleton.elim _ _
    let d : T ≅ pullback (Sigma.desc tA) (Sigma.desc tA') :=
      (Sigma.mapIso (fun z : α => prodIsoPullback (A z.1) (A' z.2))).trans
        (asIso (Sigma.desc compPull))
    let dist : T ≅ (∐ A) ⨯ (∐ A') :=
      (d.trans (pullback.congrHom htA htA')).trans
        (prodIsoPullback (∐ A) (∐ A')).symm
    let tIso : (∐ A) ⨯ (∐ A') ≅ K ⨯ K' :=
      prod.mapIso e.symm e'.symm
    let g : K'' ⟶ K ⨯ K' := hpair ≫ dist.hom ≫ tIso.hom
    have hg : Epi g := by
      let : Epi hpair := hepiPair
      let : Epi dist.hom := inferInstance
      let : Epi tIso.hom := inferInstance
      have hcomp : Epi (hpair ≫ dist.hom) := epi_comp hpair dist.hom
      let : Epi (hpair ≫ dist.hom) := hcomp
      exact epi_comp (hpair ≫ dist.hom) tIso.hom
    have hmem : K'' ∈ S := by
      let α' : Type u := ULift.{u} α
      let K''' := ∐ fun z : α' => E z.down
      let eα : K'' ≅ K''' := Sigma.reindex Equiv.ulift.symm (fun z : α' => E z.down)
      let : Fintype α' := inferInstance
      let β' : α' → Type u := fun z => β z.down
      let : ∀ z : α', Fintype (β' z) := fun _ => inferInstance
      have hmem' : K''' ∈ S := by
        simpa [K''', E, α', A] using
          (nestedFiniteCoproduct_mem (B := B) (α := α')
            (β := β')
            (X := fun z k => V z.down k.down) (fun z k => hV z.down k.down))
      obtain ⟨r, W, hW, ⟨eW⟩⟩ := hmem'
      exact ⟨r, W, hW, ⟨eα.trans eW⟩⟩
    exact ⟨K'', hmem, ⟨g, (Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi g).2 hg⟩⟩
  · intro K K' a b hK hK'
    obtain ⟨n, U, hU, ⟨e⟩⟩ := hK
    obtain ⟨n', U', hU', ⟨e'⟩⟩ := hK'
    let A : Fin n → Sheaf J (Type u) := fun i =>
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U i)
    let A' : Fin n' → Sheaf J (Type u) := fun i =>
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (U' i)
    let R := ∐ A
    let R' := ∐ A'
    let a' : R ⟶ R' := e.inv ≫ a ≫ e'.hom
    let b' : R ⟶ R' := e.inv ≫ b ≫ e'.hom
    have hLocal (u : R ⟶ R') (i : Fin n) :=
      exists_local_factor_through_finite_coproduct (V := U') (Sigma.ι A i ≫ u)
    choose S₁ hS hfa using hLocal a'
    choose T₁ hT hfb using hLocal b'
    have hCover : ∀ i : Fin n, ∃ (r : ℕ) (V : Fin r → C) (p : ∀ k, V k ⟶ U i),
        (∀ k, V k ∈ B) ∧ Sieve.ofArrows V p ∈ J (U i) ∧
          Sieve.ofArrows V p ≤ S₁ i ⊓ T₁ i := by
      intro i
      exact h_refine (U i) (hU i) (S₁ i ⊓ T₁ i)
        (J.intersection_covering (hS i) (hT i))
    choose r V p hV hVcov hVle using hCover
    have hAFactors : ∀ (i : Fin n) (k : Fin (r i)),
        ∃ (j : Fin n') (c : V i k ⟶ U' j),
          (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i k) ≫ Sigma.ι A i ≫ a' =
            (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map c ≫ Sigma.ι A' j := fun i k =>
      hfa i (p i k) (hVle i (p i k) (Sieve.ofArrows_mk (V i) (p i) k)).1
    choose ja ca hca using hAFactors
    have hBFactors : ∀ (i : Fin n) (k : Fin (r i)),
        ∃ (j : Fin n') (c : V i k ⟶ U' j),
          (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i k) ≫ Sigma.ι A i ≫ b' =
            (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map c ≫ Sigma.ι A' j := fun i k =>
      hfb i (p i k) (hVle i (p i k) (Sieve.ofArrows_mk (V i) (p i) k)).2
    choose jb cb hcb using hBFactors
    let δ := {z : Σ i : Fin n, Fin (r i) // ja z.1 z.2 = jb z.1 z.2}
    let cb' (z : δ) : V z.1.1 z.1.2 ⟶ U' (ja z.1.1 z.1.2) :=
      Eq.mp (congrArg (fun j : Fin n' => V z.1.1 z.1.2 ⟶ U' j) z.2.symm)
        (cb z.1.1 z.1.2)
    have hEqChoices : ∀ z : δ,
        ∃ (s : ℕ) (W : Fin s → C), (∀ l, W l ∈ B) ∧
          ∃ (q : ∀ l, W l ⟶ V z.1.1 z.1.2),
          ∃ hq : ∀ l, q l ≫ ca z.1.1 z.1.2 = q l ≫ cb' z,
            Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Sigma.desc fun l =>
              equalizer.lift (f := (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (ca z.1.1 z.1.2))
                (g := (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (cb' z))
                ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (q l)) (by
                  simpa only [Functor.map_comp] using
                    congrArg (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (hq l))) := by
      intro z
      rcases z with ⟨⟨i, k⟩, hij⟩
      obtain ⟨s, W, hW, q, hq, hqsurj⟩ :=
        h_equalizer (ca i k) (cb' ⟨⟨i, k⟩, hij⟩) (hV i k) (hU' (ja i k))
      exact ⟨s, W, hW, q, hq, hqsurj⟩
    choose s W hW q hq hqsurj using hEqChoices
    have hcb' (z : δ) :
        (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p z.1.1 z.1.2) ≫
            Sigma.ι A z.1.1 ≫ b' =
          (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (cb' z) ≫ Sigma.ι A' (ja z.1.1 z.1.2) := by
      rw [show (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (cb' z) ≫
          Sigma.ι A' (ja z.1.1 z.1.2) =
          (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (cb z.1.1 z.1.2) ≫
            Sigma.ι A' (jb z.1.1 z.1.2) from
          sheafifiedYoneda_map_cast_comp_sigma_ι U' z.2 (cb z.1.1 z.1.2)]
      exact hcb z.1.1 z.1.2
    let Tidx := Σ z : δ, Fin (s z)
    let X : Tidx → C := fun t => W t.1 t.2
    let L := ∐ fun t : Tidx => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (X t)
    let pK (t : Tidx) : X t ⟶ U t.1.1.1 := q t.1 t.2 ≫ p t.1.1.1 t.1.1.2
    let vK (t : Tidx) : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (X t) ⟶ K :=
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (pK t) ≫ Sigma.ι A t.1.1.1 ≫ e.inv
    have hvEq (t : Tidx) : vK t ≫ a = vK t ≫ b := by
      apply (cancel_mono e'.hom).1
      show (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (pK t) ≫ Sigma.ι A t.1.1.1 ≫ a' =
        (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (pK t) ≫ Sigma.ι A t.1.1.1 ≫ b'
      rcases t with ⟨z, l⟩
      dsimp only [pK]
      rw [Functor.map_comp]
      simp only [Category.assoc]
      calc
        (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (q z l) ≫
            ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p z.1.1 z.1.2) ≫
              Sigma.ι A z.1.1 ≫ a') =
          (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (q z l) ≫
            ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (ca z.1.1 z.1.2) ≫
              Sigma.ι A' (ja z.1.1 z.1.2)) := by rw [hca]
        _ = (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (q z l) ≫
            ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (cb' z) ≫
              Sigma.ι A' (ja z.1.1 z.1.2)) := by
              simp only [← Functor.map_comp_assoc, hq]
        _ = (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (q z l) ≫
            ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p z.1.1 z.1.2) ≫
              Sigma.ι A z.1.1 ≫ b') := by rw [hcb']
    let v (t : Tidx) : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (X t) ⟶ equalizer a b :=
      equalizer.lift (vK t) (hvEq t)
    let f : L ⟶ equalizer a b := Sigma.desc v
    have hLmem : L ∈ S :=
      coproduct_mem_finiteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda (J := J) (B := B) (γ := Tidx) X
        fun t => hW t.1 t.2
    refine ⟨L, hLmem, f, ?_⟩
    show Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J f.hom
    constructor
    intro Z y
    let x : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj Z ⟶ equalizer a b := (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J).symm y
    have hxy : Sheaf.sectionEquiv J x = y := Equiv.apply_symm_apply _ _
    rw [← hxy]
    obtain ⟨T, hT, hfactor⟩ := exists_local_factor_through_finite_coproduct
      U (x ≫ equalizer.ι a b ≫ e.hom)
    apply J.transitive hT
    intro Z₁ t ht
    rw [pullback_imageSieve_sectionEquiv]
    let x₁ : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj Z₁ ⟶ equalizer a b :=
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map t ≫ x
    obtain ⟨i, d, hd⟩ := hfactor t ht
    have hx₁ : x₁ ≫ equalizer.ι a b ≫ e.hom = (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map d ≫ Sigma.ι A i := hd
    apply J.transitive (J.pullback_stable d (hVcov i))
    intro Z₂ t₂ ht₂
    rw [pullback_imageSieve_sectionEquiv]
    let x₂ : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj Z₂ ⟶ equalizer a b :=
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map t₂ ≫ x₁
    show Presheaf.imageSieve f.hom (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J x₂) ∈ J Z₂
    obtain ⟨k, c, hc⟩ := (Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff (V i) (p i) (t₂ ≫ d)).1 ht₂
    have hx₂ : x₂ ≫ equalizer.ι a b ≫ e.hom =
        (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map c ≫
          (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i k) ≫ Sigma.ι A i := by
      calc
        x₂ ≫ equalizer.ι a b ≫ e.hom =
            (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map t₂ ≫ (x₁ ≫ equalizer.ι a b ≫ e.hom) := by
              simp only [x₂, Category.assoc]
        _ = (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map t₂ ≫
            (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map d ≫ Sigma.ι A i := by rw [hx₁]
        _ = (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map c ≫
            (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i k) ≫ Sigma.ι A i := by
          simpa only [Functor.map_comp, Category.assoc] using
            congrArg (fun g => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map g ≫ Sigma.ι A i) hc
    have heq : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (c ≫ ca i k) ≫ Sigma.ι A' (ja i k) =
        (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (c ≫ cb i k) ≫ Sigma.ι A' (jb i k) := by
      have heq' : (x₂ ≫ equalizer.ι a b ≫ e.hom) ≫ a' =
          (x₂ ≫ equalizer.ι a b ≫ e.hom) ≫ b' := by
        dsimp only [a', b']
        simp only [Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc]
        simpa only [Category.assoc] using
          congrArg (fun g => x₂ ≫ g ≫ e'.hom) (equalizer.condition a b)
      rw [hx₂] at heq'
      simp only [Category.assoc] at heq'
      rw [hca, hcb] at heq'
      simpa only [Functor.map_comp, Category.assoc] using heq'
    obtain ⟨T₂, hT₂, hequal⟩ := exists_local_eq_through_finite_coproduct U' heq
    apply J.transitive hT₂
    intro Z₃ t₃ ht₃
    rw [pullback_imageSieve_sectionEquiv]
    let x₃ : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj Z₃ ⟶ equalizer a b :=
      (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map t₃ ≫ x₂
    show Presheaf.imageSieve f.hom (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J x₃) ∈ J Z₃
    obtain ⟨hij, hab⟩ := hequal t₃ ht₃
    let z : δ := ⟨⟨i, k⟩, hij⟩
    have hdEq : (t₃ ≫ c) ≫ ca i k = (t₃ ≫ c) ≫ cb' z := by
      exact comp_eq_cast_of_heq hij (t₃ ≫ c)
        (by simpa only [Category.assoc] using hab)
    let E := equalizer ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (ca i k))
      ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (cb' z))
    let w : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj Z₃ ⟶ E :=
      equalizer.lift ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (t₃ ≫ c)) (by
        simpa only [Functor.map_comp] using congrArg (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map hdEq)
    let Q := ∐ fun l : Fin (s z) => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (W z l)
    let qE : Q ⟶ E := Sigma.desc fun l =>
      equalizer.lift ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (q z l)) (by
        simpa only [Functor.map_comp] using congrArg (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (hq z l))
    have hqE : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective qE := hqsurj z
    let jL : Q ⟶ L := Sigma.desc fun l =>
      Sigma.ι (fun t : Tidx => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).obj (X t)) ⟨z, l⟩
    have hjL : jL ≫ f ≫ equalizer.ι a b ≫ e.hom =
        qE ≫ equalizer.ι ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (ca i k))
          ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (cb' z)) ≫
          (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i k) ≫ Sigma.ι A i := by
      apply Sigma.hom_ext
      intro l
      dsimp only [jL, f, qE]
      simp only [Sigma.ι_desc_assoc, v, equalizer.lift_ι_assoc]
      simp only [vK, pK, z, Functor.map_comp, Category.assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id,
        Category.comp_id]
    have hx₃ : x₃ ≫ equalizer.ι a b ≫ e.hom =
        w ≫ equalizer.ι ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (ca i k))
          ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (cb' z)) ≫
          (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i k) ≫ Sigma.ι A i := by
      simp only [w, equalizer.lift_ι_assoc, Functor.map_comp]
      simpa only [x₃, Category.assoc] using
        congrArg (fun g => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map t₃ ≫ g) hx₂
    apply J.superset_covering _ (Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J qE.hom
      (Sheaf.sectionEquiv J w))
    intro Z₄ t₄ ht₄
    obtain ⟨w₄, hw₄⟩ := (mem_imageSieve_sectionEquiv_iff qE w t₄).1 ht₄
    apply (mem_imageSieve_sectionEquiv_iff f x₃ t₄).2
    refine ⟨w₄ ≫ jL, ?_⟩
    apply (cancel_mono (equalizer.ι a b ≫ e.hom)).1
    calc
      ((w₄ ≫ jL) ≫ f) ≫ (equalizer.ι a b ≫ e.hom) =
          w₄ ≫ (jL ≫ f ≫ equalizer.ι a b ≫ e.hom) := by
            simp only [Category.assoc]
      _ = w₄ ≫ qE ≫ equalizer.ι ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (ca i k))
          ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (cb' z)) ≫
          (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i k) ≫ Sigma.ι A i := by rw [hjL]
      _ = (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map t₄ ≫ w ≫
          equalizer.ι ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (ca i k))
          ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (cb' z)) ≫
          (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i k) ≫ Sigma.ι A i := by
            simpa only [Category.assoc] using congrArg
              (fun g => g ≫ equalizer.ι ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (ca i k))
                ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (cb' z)) ≫
                  (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map (p i k) ≫ Sigma.ι A i) hw₄
      _ = (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map t₄ ≫ x₃ ≫ equalizer.ι a b ≫ e.hom := by
        simpa only [Category.assoc] using
          (congrArg (fun g => (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map t₄ ≫ g) hx₃).symm
      _ = ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda J).map t₄ ≫ x₃) ≫ (equalizer.ι a b ≫ e.hom) := by
        simp only [Category.assoc]
  · intro K hK
    exact isQuasiCompact_of_finiteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda J B h_refine hK

